= Solution
{parent=2}

This statement is also true. The preceding compact metrizable ball $B_{X^*}$ is separable. Each ball $nB_{X^*}$ is therefore weak-star separable, and
$$
X^*=\bigcup_{n\geq1}nB_{X^*}.
$$
The union of countable dense subsets of these balls is a countable weak-star dense subset of $X^*$.

